.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt SSH3 1
.Os ssh3-c
.Sh NAME
.Nm ssh3
.Nd SSH3 client: sessions, forwards and transfers over HTTP/3 (QUIC)
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 46AqNTtVv
.Op Fl i Ar keyfile
.Op Fl l Ar login
.Op Fl p Ar port
.Op Fl L Ar [bind:]port:host:hostport
.Op Fl R Ar [bind:]port Ns Op /tcp|/udp Ns :host:port
.Op Fl D Ar [bind:]port
.Op Fl J Ar [user@]host[:port]
.Op Fl e Ar char
.Op Fl F Ar file
.Op Fl o Ar Key=Value
.Op Fl M | Fl S Ar path | Fl O Ar op
.Op Fl s Cm sftp
.Ar [user@]host[:port][/path]
.Op Ar command ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
speaks the SSH3 transport of RFC 9220: one QUIC (UDP) connection
carries an HTTP/3 extended CONNECT to the server route
.Pq default Li /ssh3-term ,
and every subsequent bidirectional stream is an SSH3 channel.
Shell and exec sessions, direct-tcp and direct-udp forwards, the
in-process sftp and the agent bridge ride those channels.
The CLI follows the
.Xr ssh 1
canon; the server counterpart is
.Xr ssh3-server 8 .
.Pp
Authentication: public keys — the Bearer JWT signed with the
.Fl i
PEM private key
.Pq ed25519, P-256 or RSA ,
OIDC id_tokens when the server is wired for them, or the Basic
step against the server's password backend.
The first connection pins the server certificate TOFU-style in
.Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
(the same store the go implementation reads).
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl 4 | Fl 6
The address family of the dial (the v4 default).
.It Fl A
Agent forwarding: the server-initiated agent-connection channels
bridge into the local agent socket.
.It Fl L Ar [bind:]port:host:hostport
Local tcp forward, repeatable; every accepted connection rides a
direct-tcp channel of the same conversation (the bind defaults to
127.0.0.1, the bracketed ipv6 bind rides).
.It Fl R Ar [bind:]port Ns Op /tcp|/udp Ns :host:port
Reverse forward, repeatable: the server binds the port and mirrors
every accepted connection or datagram back into the client-side
target (the ephemeral 0 asks the server-chosen port).
.It Fl D Ar [bind:]port
Dynamic forward, repeatable: the local listener answers SOCKS5
(SOCKS4 fallback) and bridges every target into a direct-tcp
channel.
.It Fl J Ar [user@]host[:port]
The proxy jump (one hop; the comma chain refuses — chain them by
hand or via
.Fl F ) .
.It Fl i Ar keyfile
Pubkey auth: sign the Bearer JWT with the PEM private key.
.It Fl l Ar login , Fl p Ar port
The login name (the operand user wins) and the target port (the
default 443).
.It Fl e Ar char
The escape character of the interactive session (the default ~;
at a line start: . drops, ^Z suspends, # lists the forwards, V
version, ? help, ~~ rides literal).
.It Fl F Ar file
The
.Xr ssh_config 5
file (the default ~/.ssh/config when it exists; none or
/dev/null disables): HostName, Port, User, IdentityFile,
ForwardAgent, LocalForward, RemoteForward, DynamicForward,
ProxyJump, EscapeChar, StrictHostKeyChecking, ControlMaster,
ControlPath, ControlPersist.
.It Fl o Ar Key=Value
A client option override, repeatable, case-insensitive.
.It Fl M , Fl S Ar path , Fl O Ar op
The control master, its socket path and the control ops (check,
stop, exit) against a running master.
.It Fl s Cm sftp
Serve only sftp; the put|get:local:remote specifier rides the
first word after the operand.
.It Fl n , Fl N , Fl t , Fl tt , Fl T
The stdin stays /dev/null; no session (the forwards hold the
run); force the pty (even without a local tty); never request the
pty.
.It Fl q , Fl v , Fl V
Quiet (the errors only); verbose (repeatable: -vv debug, -vvv
everything); print the version.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/.ssh3/known_hosts
The TOFU pin store of the server certificates.
.It Pa ~/.ssh/config
The OpenSSH configuration, consulted per
.Fl F .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ssh3-server 8 ,
.Xr ssh 1 ,
.Xr ssh_config 5
